WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.062
INTERVAL represents duration You can add an interval
to a date or timestamp

00:00:06.075 --> 00:00:11.816
to create a future or past point Timestamp
subtraction also returns

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:17.503
an interval Intervals are central to PostgreSQL
temporal arithmetic

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:20.358
and replace many dialect-specific date-add patterns
